<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>second day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 246 and 373-7 (R.Irani 95 not out,</p>
<p>S.Law 78, P.Prichard 56). Hampshire 161 (A.Cowan 5-49)</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Warwickshire 151 (S.Thomas 4-62) and 15-1.</p>
<p>Glamorgan 551-3 declared (H.Morris 233, A.Dale 106, S.James 83).</p>
<p>At Canterbury Kent 251 and 174-5 (T.Ward 95 not out,</p>
<p>P.DeFreitas 4-47). Derbyshire 248 (K.Krikken 61; M.McCague 5-75,</p>
<p>D.Headley 4-81)</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire 506 (G.Lloyd 102, P.Martin 78</p>
<p>not out, J.Gallian 78, G.Chapple 66, M.Watkinson 51). Durham</p>
<p>201-6 (D. Boon 85 not out).</p>
<p>At Leicester: Gloucestershire 245 (S.Young 59, R.Russell 57;</p>
<p>A. Mullally 5-52) and 8-0. Leicestershire 307 (D.Maddy 80,</p>
<p>P.Nixon 77 not out).</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Worcestershire 417 (T.Curtis 113, T.Moody</p>
<p>70, W. Weston 52; M.Bowen 5-99). Nottinghamshire 196-3</p>
<p>(P.Pollard 81, R. Robinson 80).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Somerset 463 (R.Harden 136 not out, P.Bowler</p>
<p>63, S.Herzberg 56, M N Lathwell 50). Surrey 172-7.</p>
<p>At Hove: Northamptonshire 315 (R.Montgomerie 68, D.Capel 57,</p>
<p>J. Snape 55; M.Robinson 6-78). Sussex 344-6 (N.Taylor 127,</p>
<p>K.Newell 91 not out, C.Athey 50).</p>
</text>
